---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What mesh size is standard for chilli powder?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "60–80 mesh is the standard for chilli and paprika powder — fine enough for even colour and heat distribution in seasoning blends. Coarser (20–40 mesh) is used for flakes and crushed chilli; finer (100+ mesh) for smooth sauces."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How does mesh size affect a chilli product?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Mesh sets particle size, which controls how evenly heat and colour disperse, how the powder feels on the palate, and whether it suspends smoothly in a sauce. Finer powder disperses faster and clumps less; coarser grind gives visible texture."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you grind to a custom mesh?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Mesh is adjustable to your requirement — name the mesh (or the target particle size) and we match it, documented in the quotation with the moisture and SHU specification."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Chilli Powder Mesh Size Guide (20–100 Mesh) | Tenda Peppers"
  description="Chilli powder mesh size explained — 60–80 mesh standard, coarser for flakes, finer for smooth sauces. Custom grind to requirement. China manufacturer, ISO 9001 & HACCP."
  jsonLd={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <div class="container section">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="font-size:0.9rem;color:#6b5a54;margin-bottom:16px;">
      <a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/products/dried-chillies/">Dried Chillies</a> &rsaquo; Mesh Size
    </nav>
    <h1>Chilli Powder Mesh Size Guide</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Mesh sets the particle size of chilli and paprika powder — how evenly heat and colour disperse,
      how it feels on the palate, and how it performs in a sauce or blend.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">What mesh size is standard?</h2>
    <p>
      For chilli powder and paprika, 60–80 mesh is the default: fine enough for uniform colour and
      heat in seasoning blends. The right mesh depends on the application:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Mesh</th><th>Particle character</th><th>Best for</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>20–40 mesh</td><td>Coarse, visible</td><td>Crushed chilli, flakes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>60–80 mesh</td><td>Fine, standard</td><td>Seasoning blends, general powder</td></tr>
        <tr><td>100+ mesh</td><td>Very fine</td><td>Smooth sauces, instant-mix</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">How mesh affects the product</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Dispersion</strong> — finer powder disperses faster and more evenly</li>
      <li><strong>Mouthfeel</strong> — coarser grind gives visible texture, finer is smooth</li>
      <li><strong>Clumping</strong> — finer powder clumps less and suspends better in liquid</li>
      <li><strong>Colour release</strong> — finer powder releases colour (ASTA) more readily</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">How to specify mesh</h2>
    <p>
      Name the mesh (or the target particle size) alongside your SHU window, moisture and form. Mesh
      is adjustable to requirement and documented in the quotation — for powder, 60–80 mesh is the
      sensible default unless your application says otherwise.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What mesh size is standard for chilli powder?</h3>
      <p>60–80 mesh is the standard for chilli and paprika powder — fine enough for even colour and heat distribution in seasoning blends. Coarser (20–40 mesh) is used for flakes and crushed chilli; finer (100+ mesh) for smooth sauces.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>How does mesh size affect a chilli product?</h3>
      <p>Mesh sets particle size, which controls how evenly heat and colour disperse, how the powder feels on the palate, and whether it suspends smoothly in a sauce. Finer powder disperses faster and clumps less; coarser grind gives visible texture.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Can you grind to a custom mesh?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Mesh is adjustable to your requirement — name the mesh (or the target particle size) and we match it, documented in the quotation with the moisture and SHU specification.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:32px;">
      <a class="cta" href="/contact/">Request a Specification</a>
      <a class="cta cta-outline" href="/products/dried-chillies/" style="margin-left:8px;">Dried Chillies →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
